== relational schema
Relational schema
Notation: _name_ primary key, /name/ foreign key, _/name/_ both

Students subdomain:
  StudentSecondLine : {(_StudentID_ : integer, Name : string, Email : string, category : string, /classID/ : integer)}
  Undergrad : {(_/StudentID/_ : integer)}
  Postgrad : {(_/StudentID/_ : integer)}
  StudentSecondLine_tutors_StudentSecondLine : {(/tutor/ : integer, _/tutee/_ : integer)}
Outside of any box:
  Course : {(_CourseID_ : integer, Title : string, Credits : string, _code_ : integer)}
  Assignment : {(_/CourseID/_ : integer, _/code/_ : integer, _/courseCourseID/_ : integer, _/courseCode/_ : integer, _No_ : integer, Title : string, Due : string, /courseCourseCourseID/ : integer, /courseCourseCode/ : integer)}
  Class : {(_classID_ : integer, all : string, eight : string, now : string, possible : string, /CourseID/ : integer, /code/ : integer, /courseCourseID/ : integer, /courseCode/ : integer, /No/ : integer)}
  UndergradLog : {(_undergradLogID_ : integer, with,Comma : string, italic : string)}
  SubA : {(_/undergradLogID/_ : integer)}
  SubB : {(_/undergradLogID/_ : integer)}
  StudentSecondLine_enrolls2ndLine_Course : {(_/StudentID/_ : integer, _/CourseID/_ : integer, _/code/_ : integer, _SomeNumber_ : integer, Other : string)}
  CourseTags : {(_/CourseID/_ : integer, _/code/_ : integer, _tags_ : string)}

Foreign keys
  StudentSecondLine.classID -> Class.classID
  Assignment.(CourseID, code) -> Course.(CourseID, code)
  Assignment.(courseCourseID, courseCode) -> Course.(CourseID, code)
  Assignment.(courseCourseCourseID, courseCourseCode) -> Course.(CourseID, code)
  Class.(CourseID, code, courseCourseID, courseCode, No) -> Assignment.(CourseID, code, courseCourseID, courseCode, No)
  Undergrad.StudentID -> StudentSecondLine.StudentID
  Postgrad.StudentID -> StudentSecondLine.StudentID
  SubA.undergradLogID -> UndergradLog.undergradLogID
  SubB.undergradLogID -> UndergradLog.undergradLogID
  StudentSecondLine_enrolls2ndLine_Course.StudentID -> StudentSecondLine.StudentID
  StudentSecondLine_enrolls2ndLine_Course.(CourseID, code) -> Course.(CourseID, code)
  StudentSecondLine_tutors_StudentSecondLine.tutor -> StudentSecondLine.StudentID
  StudentSecondLine_tutors_StudentSecondLine.tutee -> StudentSecondLine.StudentID
  CourseTags.(CourseID, code) -> Course.(CourseID, code)

Allowed values
  StudentSecondLine.category in {Undergrad, Postgrad}

Not enforced by the schema
  each Course has, in Enrolls 2nd line, Student Second line: at least 1
  each Course has, in has, Assignment: at least 1
  each Student Second line has, in Tutors, Student Second line: at least 1
  each Assignment has, in R2, Class: at least 1

Decisions
  Generalisation Student Second line ← Undergrad, Postgrad (id): (1) Multiple relations + categorisation attribute
  Generalisation Undergrad Log ← Sub A, Sub B (constraint not given): (1) Multiple relations, no categorisation
  Relationship Tutors (1:N): Student Second line (tutor) – Student Second line (tutee): Own relation with renamed keys

Notes
  'has' is weak without E/Id; treated as an identification dependency (Id).
  derived attribute Course.age is not stored
